# Bright MCP tool catalog

The Bright MCP server is remote and cloud-hosted — nothing runs locally. Point an
MCP-compatible client at the Bright endpoint (default `https://app.brightsec.com/mcp`) and
authenticate with your API key. Reference: https://docs.brightsec.com/docs/bright-mcp-tools

## Scans

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `runScan` | Start a scan against entrypoints. Target by `entrypointIds` or `entrypointStatuses` (`["new","changed","vulnerable"]`). Provide `tests` or `templateId`. Private targets: pass `repeaters`. |
| `getScanStatus` | Current status of a scan run. |
| `stopScan` | Stop a running scan (only when stoppable). |
| `listScans` | List scans for a project. |
| `getScanLogs` | Engine logs with severity/search/cursor filters. |
| `getScanWarnings` | Scan errors/warnings with mitigation detail. |
| `listScanVulnerabilities` | Vulnerabilities found in a scan (filter + paginate). |
| `getScanVulnerability` | Full detail for one vulnerability (evidence, reproduction). |
| `listScanEntrypoints` | Entrypoints observed during a scan (coverage/connectivity). |
| `getScanEntrypoint` | Exact request/response captured during a scan. |

## Discovery

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `runDiscovery` | Discover endpoints via `crawlerUrls` or an API def `fileId`. Private targets: pass `repeaters`. |
| `getDiscoveryStatus` | Status of a discovery run. |
| `stopDiscovery` | Stop a running discovery. |
| `listDiscoveries` | List discoveries for a project. |
| `getDiscoveryLogs` / `getDiscoveryWarnings` | Debug discovery. |
| `listDiscoveryEntrypoints` / `getDiscoveryEntrypoint` | Inspect discovery coverage and captured requests. |
| `uploadApiDefinition` | Upload an OpenAPI/Swagger file (URL or content). Returns a `fileId`. |

## Entrypoints

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `listEntrypoints` | List discovered endpoints/URLs for a project. |
| `getEntrypoint` | Full definition of one entrypoint (headers, body, config). |
| `addEntrypoint` | Manually add an entrypoint. |
| `editEntrypoint` | Update an entrypoint's request/headers/body/auth. |
| `deleteEntrypoint` | Delete an entrypoint (irreversible). |

## Vulnerabilities (project-wide)

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `listVulnerabilities` | All vulnerabilities for a project (post-scan review). |

## Authentication (see the `bright-auth` skill for the full workflow)

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `listAuths` / `getAuth` | Find/inspect auth configs. |
| `addAuth` / `editAuth` / `deleteAuth` | Manage auth objects. |
| `testAuth` | Run an auth test and return a verdict with per-result evidence. |

## Projects, tests, repeaters

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `listProjects` | Resolve the project ID before scanning. |
| `listTests` | Available security test types (SQLi, XSS, …) to pass as `tests`. |
| `listRepeaters` | Check whether a repeater is connected for private targets. |
| `createRepeater` | Create a repeater; response includes CLI args to start it. |
| `deleteRepeater` | Delete a repeater (irreversible). |

## Notes

- `entrypointStatuses` is the fastest way to scope a scan in the coding loop: `["new","changed"]`
  for iterative feedback, `["vulnerable"]` to re-verify fixes.
- Deletion tools (`deleteEntrypoint`, `deleteAuth`, `deleteRepeater`) are irreversible — confirm
  with the user before calling them.
